r_bad()` returning `None` matches this. A naive translation returning `\"helperBad string\"` would mismatch on every zero/EOF/invalid input. Recorded in `translation/ERRORS.md` along with the glibc clamp-then-truncate behavior and the `flush()`-before-`exit(0)` requirement.\n\nPhase D gate: both build, all enumerated inputs identical on all three channels, `cargo test` passes, no `#[ignore]`/skipped tests (verified `grep -c` = 0), and `c_src/` is unmodified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1032,"cache_read_input_tokens":36867,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1032,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64d1a727-66b8-4199-9cb5-ac7b5856a01d","uuid":"1f69109e-16b4-4b64-91dd-93587e3f7551","timestamp":"2026-08-28T12:38:10.121Z"}
